cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper and the software as below."
title: "SPECTRUM: global mean sea-level forecast"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Minchew
    given-names: Brent
    affiliation: "California Institute of Technology"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bminchew/spectrum-gmsl"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - sea level
  - sea-level rise
  - forecasting
  - Bayesian inference
  - ice sheets
  - glaciers
  - thermal expansion
abstract: >-
  Code that produces the numbers and figures in "A Data-Driven,
  Component-Level Projection Framework for 21st-Century Sea-Level Rise".
  SPECTRUM forecasts global mean sea level to 2100 by modeling each
  contributor separately, calibrating the models against observational
  records where they exist, and summing the components over a
  10,000-member ensemble. Observed global mean sea level is withheld from
  every calibration and used to test the sum.
